-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1, PART 1: CONTRACTS TO WHICH THE ACT APPLIES (s 1).
-- s 1(2) to (4) say which sections the Schedule modifies; the modifying windows are in soga-schedule, soga-part7-supplementary
-- and soga-interpretation, and the functions here gather them by section (E1 option B, hand-gathered; see the fork register).
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on
-- these facts".  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`
IMPORT `soga-part7-supplementary`
IMPORT `soga-interpretation`
IMPORT `soga-schedule`

DECLARE `Section of the Act that refers to the Schedule` IS ONE OF
    `section 11(3)`
    `section 12`
    `section 13(3)`
    `section 14`
    `section 15`
    `section 35`
    `section 55`
    `section 56`
    `the definition of business in section 61(1)`
    `a section with no reference to the Schedule`

§ `Part 1 -- Contracts to which Act applies`

-- s 1(1).
-- src:189 | 1.—(1) This Act applies to contracts of sale of goods made on or
-- src:190 | after (but not to those made before) 1 January 1894.
@ref s 1(1) (src:189-190)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 1(1) this Act applies to the contract of sale of goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 1894)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Act applies to contracts of sale of goods made on or after (but not to those made before) 1 January 1894."
            JUST FALSE

-- s 1(2), gathered by hand (E1 option B) from the windows of the Schedule and ss 55(3), 56 and 61(5).
-- src:192 | (2) In relation to contracts made on certain dates, this Act applies
-- src:193 | subject to the modification of certain of its sections as mentioned in
-- src:194 | the Schedule.
@ref s 1(2) (src:192-194)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `the section` IS A `Section of the Act that refers to the Schedule`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 1(2) this Act applies to the contract subject to the modification of the section mentioned in the Schedule` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 1894))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Schedule affects a contract made before 1 January 1894." (Schedule paragraph 1(3)), and s 1(1) says the Act does not apply to such a contract.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the section`
            WHEN `section 11(3)` THEN `s 11(5) paragraph 2 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made`
            WHEN `section 12` THEN `s 12(6) paragraph 3 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made`
            WHEN `section 13(3)` THEN `s 13(4) paragraph 4 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made`
            WHEN `section 14` THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF `s 14(6) paragraph 5 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 14(6) paragraph 6 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE
                        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to contracts made on certain dates"; paragraphs 5 and 6 give the dates for section 14. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
                        JUST FALSE
            WHEN `section 15` THEN `s 15(3) paragraph 7 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made`
            WHEN `section 35` THEN `s 35(8) paragraph 8 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made`
            WHEN `section 55` THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF `s 55(3) paragraph 9 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 55(3) paragraph 10 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE
                        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to contracts made on certain dates"; s 55(3) gives the dates for section 55. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
                        JUST FALSE
            WHEN `section 56` THEN `s 56 paragraph 11 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was made`
            WHEN `the definition of business in section 61(1)` THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF `s 61(5) paragraph 12 of the Schedule applies as regards the definition of business` `the date the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 61(5) paragraph 13 of the Schedule applies as regards the definition of business` `the date the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE
                        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to contracts made on certain dates"; s 61(5) gives the dates for the definition of business. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
                        JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) speaks of "certain of its sections"; subsection (4) answers a section with no reference.
            WHEN `a section with no reference to the Schedule` THEN NOTHING

-- s 1(3).
-- src:196 | (3) Any such modification is indicated in the section concerned by a
-- src:197 | reference to the Schedule.
@ref s 1(3) (src:196-197)
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Section of the Act that refers to the Schedule`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 1(3) a modification of the section is indicated in the section by a reference to the Schedule` IS
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `a section with no reference to the Schedule` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) says a modification "is indicated in the section concerned by a reference to the Schedule"; it does not say that a section with no reference is unmodified (subsection (4) does).
        NOTHING
    WHEN `section 11(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `section 12` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `section 13(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `section 14` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `section 15` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `section 35` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `section 55` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `section 56` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the definition of business in section 61(1)` THEN JUST TRUE

-- s 1(4).
-- src:202 | (4) Accordingly, where a section does not contain such a reference,
-- src:203 | this Act applies in relation to the contract concerned without such
-- src:204 | modification of the section.
@ref s 1(4) (src:202-204)
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Section of the Act that refers to the Schedule`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 1(4) this Act applies in relation to the contract without modification of the section` IS
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `a section with no reference to the Schedule` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (4) applies "where a section does not contain such a reference"; for a section that does contain one, s 1(2) and the Schedule decide. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `section 11(3)` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see section 11(3). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `section 12` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see section 11(3). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `section 13(3)` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see section 11(3). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `section 14` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see section 11(3). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `section 15` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see section 11(3). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `section 35` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see section 11(3). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `section 55` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see section 11(3). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `section 56` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see section 11(3). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
    WHEN `the definition of business in section 61(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
